<title>GERMANY: ALPINE SKIING-MAIER WINS WORLD CUP SUPER-G.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-MAIER WINS WORLD CUP SUPER-G.</headline>
<dateline>GARMISCH-PARTENKIRCHEN, Germany 1997-02-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Austria's Hermann Maier won the fourth men's super-G of the World Cup Alpine skiing season on Sunday when he clocked one minute 21.64 seconds, according to provisional results.  </p>
<p>Italy's Kristian Ghedina was second in 1.22.16 with Norwegians Lasse Kjus and Atle Skaardal joint third in 1:22.25.</p>
</text>
